# Two normalized pairs l <= x y <= h from one product by mul_2_2: its second limb moved down and
# up by the bound d of the product's own error, and each pair renormalized exactly. The lower
# limb is RD(z1 - d) written as -RU(d - z1), so that no fused result is negated (a rule of the
# generator): what is negated is z1, from the renormalization of mul_2_2 (a subtraction), and the
# result of add_up_1, a select; d is used as it is on both sides. The values are those of
# sub_down_1(z1, d), rounding to nearest being symmetric.
kernel:        mul_dir_2_2
input:         x = x0 x1
input:         y = y0 y1
output:        l = l0 l1
output:        h = h0 h1
value:         x*y
requires:      normalized x
requires:      normalized y
ensures:       normalized l
ensures:       normalized h
ensures:       outward l below rel=(2*(1+u)^3*up((1+u)^6)*up(unit(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2)))+2*u^2)*(1+unit(mul_2_2))/(1-u) abs=2*(1+u)^2*(1/2*up((1+u)^6)*eta+up((1+u)*(2*(1+u)^5*eta+tiny(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2))+eta/2)+eta/(2*u)))+eta+(2*(1+u)^3*up((1+u)^6)*up(unit(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2)))+2*u^2)/(1-u)*tiny(mul_2_2)
ensures:       outward h above rel=(2*(1+u)^3*up((1+u)^6)*up(unit(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2)))+2*u^2)*(1+unit(mul_2_2))/(1-u) abs=2*(1+u)^2*(1/2*up((1+u)^6)*eta+up((1+u)*(2*(1+u)^5*eta+tiny(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2))+eta/2)+eta/(2*u)))+eta+(2*(1+u)^3*up((1+u)^6)*up(unit(mul_2_2)/(1-unit(mul_2_2)))+2*u^2)/(1-u)*tiny(mul_2_2)
min_precision: 4
source:        mul_2_2 moved down and up by the bound of its own error, renormalized exactly (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
theorem:       proofs/theories/Directed2.v mul_dir_2_2_correct
status:        proved
cone_exempt:   through the directed sums and two_sum_ord, which select; the interval kernels test l0 and h0

(z0, z1, d) = mul_ball_2_2(x0, x1, y0, y1)
nz          = neg(z1)
t           = add_up_1(d, nz)
wl          = neg(t)
wu          = add_up_1(z1, d)
(l0, l1)    = two_sum_ord(z0, wl)
(h0, h1)    = two_sum_ord(z0, wu)
